From: Nuvoton OpenBMC <noreply@nuvoton.com>
Subject: [PATCH] fix build/integration issues for this distro's sdbusplus and mctpd

Three independent fixes needed to build and run NVIDIA's Core-26.05-1_br
spdm daemon against this distro's stack:

1. NVIDIA's Core-26.05-1_br branch is written against
   sdbusplus::message::object_path and sdbusplus::bus::bus, which are the
   spellings from an older sdbusplus. The version currently pinned by
   meta-phosphor's sdbusplus recipe has already renamed these to
   sdbusplus::object_path and sdbusplus::bus_t (the old spellings no
   longer exist / are deprecated-as-error under -Werror). This is a
   mechanical rename only, to the exact same underlying types, so it is
   safe against any sdbusplus version that has them.

2. Under -Ddiscovery_only_from_mctp_control=enabled,
   mctpNewObjectSignal() in mctp_endpoint_discovery.cpp references an
   `invPath` local that is only declared in the (disabled)
   Inventory.Item.SPDMResponder-matching branch, so it fails to compile.
   Declares an empty sdbusplus::object_path in its place, which is the
   correct "no inventory object" value for that build configuration.

3. getBindingType() requires xyz.openbmc_project.MCTP.Binding on the
   MCTP endpoint object, aborting discovery for every endpoint if it's
   absent. codeconstruct's mctpd (au.com.codeconstruct.MCTP1, what this
   distro's mctpd.service actually runs) never exposes that interface on
   endpoint objects, so every endpoint discovery was silently dropped
   with "Unable to get binding type". bindingType is purely informational
   (stored on the Responder dbus object; used only for duplicate-responder
   comparison, never for transport selection), so fall back to a fixed
   value when the interface is absent, mirroring the fallback
   getMediumType() already has for the same situation.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [layer-local: adapts an out-of-tree
fork's build to this distro's pinned sdbusplus version and mctpd
implementation; not applicable upstream]

